From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Elsbrock <simon@iodev.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:45:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gpio, regulator: add the Echo Dot (5th gen) CPLD and MT6395
 PMIC, ported to 6.12

Two self-contained Amazon drivers from the 5.4 release (ADR 0035):
- gpio-amzncpld, the SLG4BZ45165 CPLD GPIO expander the volume, action and
  mute buttons hang off. The gpiolib irqchip is migrated to 6.12's model: the
  irq is set up through gpio_chip.irq before gpiochip_add_data (selecting
  GPIOLIB_IRQCHIP), and the removed gpiochip_irqchip_add() /
  gpiochip_set_chained_irqchip() calls are dropped; its own threaded handler
  still demuxes into the domain.
- mt6395-regulator, the MT6395 PMIC.

Both take the 6.12 i2c probe (no id argument; fetched with
i2c_client_get_device_id) and void remove. Off in every current variant.
---
 drivers/gpio/Kconfig                 |   9 +
 drivers/gpio/Makefile                |   1 +
 drivers/gpio/gpio-amzncpld.c         | 875 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/regulator/Kconfig            |   7 +
 drivers/regulator/Makefile           |   1 +
 drivers/regulator/mt6395-regulator.c | 936 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 1829 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpio/gpio-amzncpld.c
 create mode 100644 drivers/regulator/mt6395-regulator.c

diff --git a/drivers/gpio/Kconfig b/drivers/gpio/Kconfig
index d93cd4f72..5c33596ac 100644
--- a/drivers/gpio/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/gpio/Kconfig
@@ -1930,3 +1930,12 @@ config GPIO_VIRTUSER
 endmenu
 
 endif
+
+config GPIO_AMZNCPLD
+	tristate "Amazon CPLD GPIO expander (MT8519 Echo)"
+	depends on I2C && OF
+	select GPIOLIB_IRQCHIP
+	help
+	  GPIO expander behind the Amazon CPLD (SLG4BZ45165) on the Echo Dot
+	  (5th gen); the volume and action buttons and the microphone switch
+	  hang off it.
diff --git a/drivers/gpio/Makefile b/drivers/gpio/Makefile
